          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Capacity and Continuous Output</h3>

          <p>
            Two numbers in that table decide most purchases. Capacity tells you how long a load runs; continuous output tells you which loads can run at all. A 2,000W unit cannot start a 2,500W well pump no matter how full its battery is, and a 6,000W unit with an empty battery runs nothing. Size output to your single largest starting load first, then size capacity to the hours you need.
          </p>

