        <!-- FAQ -->
        <div id="faq" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            11. Frequently Asked Questions
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the best Anker power station for most people?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                The SOLIX C1000 Gen 2. It stores 1,024Wh, runs 2,000W loads, recharges from a wall outlet in about 49 minutes and weighs around 25 lb. That covers camping, CPAP, a refrigerator through a short outage and most kitchen appliances. If the original C1000 is discounted by more than about $100, it is the better value buy.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the Anker power plant?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                There is no Anker product sold as a power plant in the US. People use the phrase for Anker's large home backup batteries, which in practice means the SOLIX F3800 Plus or a pair of F3000 units. The F3800 Plus is the one that delivers 240V output, 6,000W and expansion to about 26.9kWh per unit.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is the Anker SOLIX C1000 worth buying in 2026?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Yes, especially on sale. It holds 1,056Wh, outputs 1,800W, refills in about 58 minutes in UltraFast mode and can be expanded to 2,112Wh with the BP1000. The C1000 Gen 2 is lighter and more powerful, but the original remains one of the best values in the category whenever it is discounted.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can the Anker SOLIX F3800 run a whole house?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                It can run a large share of one. The F3800 Plus delivers 6,000W at 120V or 240V, enough for a well pump, fridge, furnace and lights together. With expansion batteries and solar it can cover multi-day outages. Central air plus an electric range and dryer at once would exceed it, so prioritize circuits.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the difference between the Anker C300X and C300X DC?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Both hold 288Wh of LiFePO4 with two 140W USB-C ports. The standard C300X adds a 300W AC inverter with outlets and weighs about 8.8 lb. The C300X DC removes the inverter, keeping only USB and car-socket outputs, and weighs around 6.2 lb. Buy the DC version only if nothing you own needs a wall plug.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Are Anker power stations better than EcoFlow?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Neither is better across the board. Anker leads on charging speed, compact weight and its standard 5-year warranty. EcoFlow offers a larger ecosystem of extra batteries, smart panels and a highly rated app. At the 1,000Wh level they trade wins model by model, so compare current prices and the specific features you need.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How long does an Anker battery last?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Current SOLIX models use LiFePO4 cells rated for 3,000 to 4,000 cycles before dropping to 80% capacity. One full cycle a day for eight years would still be within that range, and most owners cycle far less. Store it partly charged in a cool place and top it up every three months.
              </p>
            </div>

          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Common Mistakes -->
        <div id="mistakes" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            12. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying by model number instead of by job</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                The number after C or F roughly tracks capacity, not suitability. A C800 Plus is a better camping battery than a C1000, and a C2000 Gen 2 is a better RV battery than an F2000 despite the same capacity. Decide what you need to run, for how long, then pick the model.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Expecting a 120V unit to run 240V appliances</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                No C-series unit and no single F3000 can run a well pump, central air condenser, electric dryer or water heater wired for 240V. If any of those are on your outage list, the F3800 Plus or a paired F3000 is the only Anker option, and it needs proper wiring.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Paying full price for a renamed PowerHouse</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                The SOLIX F2000 is the PowerHouse 767 with a new label. It is still a good battery, but newer models like the C2000 Gen 2 hold the same 2,048Wh in a much lighter box with faster charging. Buy the older unit only at a real discount.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Fast charging on a busy circuit</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                HyperFlash charging pulls close to the full capacity of a 15-amp circuit. Plug the battery into a kitchen outlet while the microwave runs and the breaker will trip. Use a free circuit, or set a lower charging rate in the Anker app when speed does not matter.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying an expansion battery before you need one</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Expansion packs only fit specific Anker models and add weight and cost. Most owners find that fast AC or solar recharging covers their real outages. Use the base unit through one season, note how often it actually runs empty, then decide whether extra capacity is worth it.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

