        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most buyers, the best Anker power station is the SOLIX C1000 Gen 2: 1,024Wh, 2,000W and a refill in under an hour, in a box one person can carry. If the original C1000 is on a deep discount, it does nearly the same job for less. Campers should look at the C800 Plus, laptop and phone users at the C300X, and anyone who wants overnight capacity without the weight of the F series at the C2000 Gen 2.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For real home backup, skip the middle and go straight to the F3800 Plus with a properly installed Home Power Panel or transfer switch, or start with an F3000 if your home has no 240V loads you need to keep running. Whatever you buy, size it to your largest starting load first and your outage hours second, and do not pay full price for an older PowerHouse model wearing a new SOLIX label.
